# ABOUTME: Template for the two credentials wowperf needs to reach the Warcraft Logs API.
# ABOUTME: Copy this file to `.env` and fill both values in; that copy is gitignored.
#
# Create your own API client at https://www.warcraftlogs.com/api/clients/
# Any name and any redirect URL will do -- the client credentials flow uses neither.
#
# One client per person. RPGLogs' terms prohibit holding several to multiply the
# hourly point budget, and one client's budget is far more than a run costs: the
# limit reads 3600 points an hour and a full run fetch spends roughly six.
#
# These credentials read public and unlisted reports. A report set to private on
# Warcraft Logs needs a login this tool does not implement, so make yours unlisted
# rather than private if you do not want it in the rankings.

WCL_CLIENT_ID=
WCL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The subjects the end-to-end suite runs against. `uv run pytest` ignores these;
# only `uv run pytest -m e2e` reads them, and it fails with instructions rather
# than guessing when they are unset.
#
# Both name report cW38jmwdnZfbHVL4, which CLAUDE.md records as the raid the
# end-to-end tests use. Fight 2 is a 20-player Heroic kill of Nek'zali the
# Soulcoiler; fight 30 is the deepest of that night's eight attempts at Ula'tek,
# 480s ending at 16.49% boss health. The wipe is the long attempt on purpose: a
# short one reaches too few of the analysers to be worth a live run.
#
# The twenty players on this report are real people. Refer to them by class,
# spec, role or index -- never by name -- in code, tests, commits and documents.

WOWPERF_E2E_RAID_KILL=https://www.warcraftlogs.com/reports/cW38jmwdnZfbHVL4#fight=2
WOWPERF_E2E_RAID_WIPE=https://www.warcraftlogs.com/reports/cW38jmwdnZfbHVL4#fight=30
